lantern-pr 1
# 29
#title Update Lantern by itself on macOS, announce releases elsewhere
#url https://github.com/MobileReality/lantern/pull/29
#branch feat/auto-update
#base main
#opened 2026-11-10
#head 6ea43c929cc35a3d0f52972a9dd812fc68affc6a
#describe what An installed Lantern finds a newer release by itself. On a Mac it downloads the update and installs it only when no editor terminal, running process or run started by Lantern would be ended; elsewhere it shows a notice with a link to the release page.
#describe what Sessions that run outside Lantern, such as in iTerm, do not hold the update back, because a restart does not end them.
#describe what Adds a Check for Updates item, a setting to switch the checks off, and a docs page on what each check sends. The Mac feed answers 404 until the release asset is renamed to include arm64, so for now that path is a quiet no-op.
#describe before New releases were found and installed by hand.
#describe after A Mac shows Update ready: restart when your sessions finish, installs when no terminal or run it would end is alive, and asks for confirmation naming what a Restart now would end.
#describe verified Typecheck, lint and the full test suite pass. The update flow itself was never run.
